          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "Thin, narrow, flat pieces of wood used for many purposes, such as in constructing lattices of trellis work, Venetian blinds, or to form a groundwork upon which to fasten the slates or tiles of a roof or the plaster of a wall or ceiling. For groundwork of any material upon which plaster or another such material is applied, use \"lath (grounding surface).\" [Source: Getty AAT]"
    }
